{"id": "EUVD-2026-59251", "enisaUuid": "5066ead5-70a8-368e-8889-b13d779a5e25", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: bpf: Fix hid_bpf_get_data() range check\n\nhid_bpf_get_data() returns a pointer into the HID-BPF context data when\nthe caller-provided offset and size fit inside ctx->allocated_size.\n\nThe current check adds rdwr_buf_size and offset before comparing the\nresult against ctx->allocated_size. Since both values are unsigned, a\nvery large size can wrap the sum below ctx->allocated_size and make the\nhelper return a pointer even though the requested range is not contained\nin the backing buffer.\n\nUse check_add_overflow() to reject wrapped range ends before comparing\nthe requested range end against ctx->allocated_size.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:55:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:44:39", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f72176bde0cc0e709e41ab170c71e8f229232af6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ca373549140dfb386aa2de38364b58441b1f4885", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/61a959b82f1aecd6d2d35c208013dd077cac9d10", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f81bc5a709dcbaf2a3bbef4ca7167f93900cc39f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2d044049421dd48212b28646a850749d4a2d57fa"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p43j-9ghf-j8hh", "CVE-2026-72352"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1365e47b-71c4-3664-b8b3-e26bd14ef81c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "658ee5a64fcfbbf758447fa3af425729eaabb0dc <f81bc5a709dcbaf2a3bbef4ca7167f93900cc39f"}, {"id": "16f3bf17-6bb1-3f03-9e8d-ae8ca09d03e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "658ee5a64fcfbbf758447fa3af425729eaabb0dc <61a959b82f1aecd6d2d35c208013dd077cac9d10"}, {"id": "18548d9c-1480-3470-ac9f-2874b06e8fc5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "187dc5dd-ddf4-3a36-a112-9ced1aef6f57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "658ee5a64fcfbbf758447fa3af425729eaabb0dc <ca373549140dfb386aa2de38364b58441b1f4885"}, {"id": "1bf77b92-ff68-3f06-aa74-800064af973a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5ca50e7a-6cc5-3689-bcbf-818efa73e542", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "702f4223-588e-322d-a087-ff66df79acb5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "79309094-2a37-3fa6-8fbe-a4ca4de54120", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "658ee5a64fcfbbf758447fa3af425729eaabb0dc <2d044049421dd48212b28646a850749d4a2d57fa"}, {"id": "958ee9f4-78ae-3b6b-a1df-fa19a92f01bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "b9b142f0-a8f9-3d38-be5f-d2d9a4b5ea42", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.3"}, {"id": "ce8577e9-dd49-35b3-aa81-9cf9ddfb36f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "f4469d7d-67c2-31a7-88e1-97e0fbdedcb3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "658ee5a64fcfbbf758447fa3af425729eaabb0dc <f72176bde0cc0e709e41ab170c71e8f229232af6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fe668c60-c93f-3c33-a86f-96732558fbe9", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}